      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Marketing Communications Content Specialist Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2361 # of Openings: 1 POSITION TITLE: Marketing Communications Content Specialist DEPARTMENT: Office of Marketing and Communications REPORTS TO: Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications POSITION TYPE: 80% Remote PRIMARY PURPOSE/POSITION SUMMARY Develop, research, write, edit and strategically manage and produce editorial and marketing content across a variety of platforms with a focus on content creation for web, social media and advertising that advances and promotes the mission of Dominican University while ensuring brand consistency, audience engagement and alignment with institutional communications goals. EXPECTATIONS FOR ALL DOMINICAN EMPLOYEES To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, to give compassionate service, and to participate in the creation of a more just and humane world. JOB COMPONENTS/PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Create engaging, informative and persuasive editorial and marketing content for both print and digital platforms within Dominican University's distinct brand voice Develop compelling content and copy for university marketing and advertising campaigns across multiple channels, including student recruitment campaigns, landing pages, email communications and website content. Contribute to and execute content for all university social media channels, including day-to-day posting and scheduling as well as long-term content planning, with a focus on capturing and creating engaging short-form video content for platforms such as Instagram and TikTok. Manage and mentor a team of student content creators, including assigning projects, providing creative direction and ensuring content aligns with university brand standards and strategic goals. Identify and respond to emerging social media trends, platform best practices and audience engagement opportunities to grow reach and engagement across university channels. Manage projects through the full creative process, from initial assignment and concepting through drafting, revision and final production Edit and proofread content to ensure high editorial standards and brand consistency are met across all communications. Review marketing materials produced by university colleges, schools and departments to ensure adherence to brand voice and institutional style. Support the writing and editing needs of campus clients as required. Perform other duties as assigned. COMPETENCIES: (Required knowledge, skills, abilities) Proven ability to write and develop action-focused editorial and marketing content within a distinct brand voice. Knowledge of and experience with social media platforms and content production, digital content best practices and emerging trends in content marketing. Excellent writing, editing and proofreading skills with a keen and diligent eye for detail, language, flow and grammar. Ability to work independently, manage competing priorities and meet tight deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE 3-5 years experience in copywriting at a demonstrably high level of quality. Demonstrated experience managing or contributing to social media channels and creating digital content across multiple platforms. Bachelor's degree in English, Journalism, Communications, Marketing or a related field. Experience in higher education is preferred, but not required. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Ability to spend long durations of the workday sitting at a desk and working on a computer Must be able to lift up to 15 pounds at times SALARY AND FLSA STATUS Salary: $50,000 - $53,000 annually FLSA Status: Exempt (Salaried), Full-time (at least 37.5 hours per week) BENEFITS Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance Retirement plan with employer matching contributions Professional development opportunities Tuition remission for employees and their dependents Flexible spending accounts (FSA) Generous paid time off (PTO) Employment at Dominican University is contingent upon the successful completion of a background investigation. About Dominican University Dominican University is a Catholic, comprehensive teaching university located in River Forest, a suburb of Chicago, with an additional campus in the Pilsen neighborhood of Chicago. Accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Dominican University offers associate, baccalaureate, master’s, and doctoral degrees. It is highly regarded for its academic rigor, thoughtful accompaniment of students, intentional affordability, and values-based, relationship-centered learning environment. Dominican currently enrolls over 3,800 students, including 2,690 undergraduates and 1,114 graduate students. Sixty-eight percent (68%) of undergraduate students identify as Latinx, 5% as Black or African American, and 3% as Asian. Under-represented minority students comprise 77% of the undergraduate enrollment and 38% of the graduate enrollment. Over 90 percent of undergraduates receive some form of financial aid. Nearly half of all undergraduates are first-generation college students; over half are federal Pell Grant recipients, illustrating their families’ level of income; and 58% are eligible for low-income MAP grants from the State of Illinois. Recognized since 2011 as a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) by the U.S. Department of Education, Dominican is committed to expanding and enhancing educational opportunities for Latinx students and all students from historically underrepresented groups. For more information, visit www.dom.edu . Expectations for all Dominican Employees: To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, give compassionate service, and participate in the creation of a more just and humane world, engage in university service work that promotes collaboration and community building. This includes participating in organizational initiatives, supporting campus events, contributing to community outreach, and fostering a diverse and inclusive environment through involvement in various staff-driven activities and groups. Institutional Statement Dominican University is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive academic community. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Dominican University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and protected veterans. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
