      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Alumnae/i Relations Student Ambassador Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2376 # of Openings: 1 TITLE: Alumnae/i Relations Student Ambassador DEPARTMENT: University Advancement OPEN TO: Dominican University Undergraduate Students FLSA STATUS: Hourly HOURLY RATE: 15.00 DATE AVAILABLE: August 2026 - May 2027 Duties and Responsibilities Assist with general alumnae/i inquiries via phone, email, mail, etc., and direct them to the appropriate office Support administrative office tasks, i.e. answering phones, various filing, special projects, etc. Aid in management of the University Advancement database through tracking alumnae/i activities and information updates Check alumnae/i page on LinkedIn for updates and new members. Support the University’s death notice process by researching obituaries, tracking information, and mailing invitations for two remembrance masses Proof various letters, mailings, and other print materials for publication Prepare large mailings to alumnae/i Provide campus tours to DU alumnae/i upon request Other projects as assigned by supervisor Greet visitors to the Office of Alumnae/i Relations and/or University Advancement Assist with the execution of events including, but not limited to: Reunion activities, Homecoming, Benefit, Memorial Mass, Holiday Sing, etc. Required Qualifications: Must be enrolled as a full-time undergraduate student in Fall 2026 – Spring 2027 semesters Must be in good conduct standing with the Dean of Students If concerned about this, please email (dperez1@dom.edu) Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to be discreet and keep alumnae/i information confidential Strong written and oral communication skills Ability to multi-task and switch priorities quickly and seamlessly Ability to work autonomously and in a group setting Flexibility and creativity May be required to assist with evening/weekend programs Willingness to learn and perform new tasks Knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite A sense of humor Anticipated Skills you will Build: Interpersonal office skills that will translate to any professional environment Basic database searches and data management Functions of a Development office, i.e. limited fundraising, constituent management, etc. And so much more! Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
