    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78859e9fd3bb2501a034de83b0012f&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: DUPAC Ambassador – Social Media Marketing Focus Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2381 # of Openings: 1 Positio n : DUPAC Ambassador – Social Media Marketing Focus Location: Dominican University Performing Arts Center Reports To: Marketing & Events Coordinator Hourly Rate: $15.00 Overview Are you passionate about the performing arts and love connecting with audiences online? The Dominican University Performing Arts Center (DUPAC) is seeking enthusiastic and creative DUPAC Ambassadors with a strong interest in social media marketing. As a DUPAC Ambassador, you will play an essential role in promoting our diverse programming—including nationally touring artists, cultural events, and beloved family productions like The Nutcracker Ballet—while gaining valuable hands-on experience in arts marketing, customer service, and event operations. Key Responsibilities Social Media Marketing & Content Creation Lead and assist with social media campaigns across platforms such as Instagram, Facebook, and TikTok to engage and grow our audience. Create original content (photos, videos, stories, and posts) that highlights upcoming performances, behind-the-scenes moments, and the DUPAC experience. Host social media takeovers to give followers an insider’s view of events and daily operations. Collaborate with the marketing team to brainstorm and implement innovative promotional strategies. Monitor engagement and trends to help refine our digital outreach and maximize impact. Event Support & Customer Service Assist patrons with ticket sales both online and by phone, providing excellent customer service and troubleshooting any issues. Support front-of-house operations: welcome guests, scan and sell tickets, and maintain a polished, organized environment before and after each show. Provide backstage assistance as needed, including helping performers, coordinating with stage managers, and learning basic light and sound cue operations. Operations & Teamwork Ensure the venue is clean, organized, and ready for events. Work collaboratively with staff across departments to ensure seamless event execution. Participate in ongoing professional development and training sessions. Qualifications Strong interest in social media marketing and the performing arts Excellent written and verbal communication skills Creative thinker with an eye for engaging content Comfortable using major social media platforms (Instagram, Facebook, TikTok) Friendly, reliable, and eager to learn Ability to work evenings and weekends as needed for events Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b019ff7257dbf68fe&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Enterprise Applications Student Assistant Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2374 # of Openings: 1 POSITION TITLE: Enterprise Applications Student Assistant DEPARTMENT: Information Technology REPORTS TO: Assistant Director of Systems Integrations JOB STATUS: Part-time, Undergraduate Assistant DATE AVAILABLE: 8/24/2026 LOCATION: River Forest HOURS PER WEEK: 15 HOURLY RATE: $15.00/hourly TERM: One year term, with possible extension for additional year(s) Position Summary The Enterprise Applications Student Assistant (EASA) works with Information Technology staff and the Dominican University community on projects related to records management, information governance, enterprise applications, and data analytics. The EASA will move boxes, sort records, alphabetize, and inventory paper and digital assets across the university. The EASA will prepare and scan records into the electronic content management system (Softdocs etrieve) and index records. The EASA handles and accesses confidential information in all departments throughout the university. Duties & Responsibilities Supervisory Scope: This role does not supervise employees. Assist in performing records inventory for university departments, including moving boxes and preparing records for off-site storage (sorting, organizing, alphabetizing, etc.). Assist in implementing Softdocs™ across the university, including preparing physical records for digitizing, scanning paper records, uploading electronic records, indexing records, and updating metadata. Potential to assist in designing digital forms & workflows for university departments. Potential to assist with other web & desktop applications. Potential to assist with data analytics projects. Participate in other DU-IT projects as assigned. Required Qualifications Enrollment in a Dominican University undergraduate program is required. Ability to lift & carry boxes up to 50 pounds occasionally. Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, etc.). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills. Ability to work collaboratively within a group and independently. Ability to manage your time effectively to meet deadlines. DESIRED Education and Experience Courses in computer science, informatics, web design, programming, data analysis, or statistics. Knowledge of web & desktop applications used in an academic setting. Experience working in Records Management or Information Governance fields. Experience working with content management systems like Softdocs™ or Drupal. Experience working with coding languages/tools like HTML, SQL, JSON, Power Apps/Automate. Experience working with data analytics tools like Tableau, Power BI, or Google Analytics. Experience working with artificial intelligence like Claude, Google Gemini, or ChatGPT. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b019ff730c4d56eb5&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Graphic Design Intern Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2375 # of Openings: 1 JOB TITLE: Graphic Design Intern DEPARTMENT: Office of Alumnae/i Relations PAY RATE: $15/hour for up to 15 hours/week REPORTS TO: Assistant Director of Alumnae/i Relations DATES: 2025-2026 School Year Summary The Office of Alumnae/i Relations is committed to fostering meaningful and lasting connections between the department and its diverse alumnae/i community. Through programs, events, and communications, we strive to celebrate alumnae/i achievements, support lifelong engagement, and encourage alumnae/i involvement. The Graphic Design Intern will support this mission by enhancing the visual identity of the office through the creation of engaging and consistent marketing materials for a wide range of alumnae/i-related initiatives and events. Primary Responsibilities Design promotional materials and event graphics for use on social media, email campaigns, web platforms, and print Create branded items such as stickers, buttons, signage, and event collateral that reflect the identity of the Office of Alumnae/i Relations Ensure visual consistency across all digital and print materials produced by the office Collaborate with staff to conceptualize and execute marketing campaigns for alumnae/i events, programs, and outreach initiatives Provide design and logistical support for major events and ongoing programming Attend team meetings and regular check-ins with supervisor Other duties as assigned Required Competencies Creativity and proficiency in graphic design software (e.g., Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, etc.) Strong organizational, written, and verbal communication skills Ability to take initiative and work independently on projects Collaborative mindset and willingness to contribute ideas Serves as a positive representative of the office and the College Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b019ff7144e2c6121&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Introductory Organic Chemistry Laboratory  Assistant Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2373 # of Openings: 0 TITLE: CHEM 104 – Introductory Organic Chemistry Laboratory  Assistant FLSA Status: Hourly REPORTS TO: Senior Lecturer OPEN TO: Undergraduate Students AVAILABLE: Fall 2026 HOURLY RATE: 15.00 The Student Laboratory Assistant provides instructional and technical support for the CHEM 104 Introductory Organic Chemistry laboratory. Working under the supervision of the laboratory instructor, the assistant helps maintain a safe, organized, and efficient learning environment while assisting students in developing fundamental laboratory skills used in introductory organic chemistry. Responsibilities Include: Prepare laboratory workstations before each laboratory session. Assemble, distribute, and collect laboratory equipment, chemicals, and supplies. Assist with laboratory setup, demonstrations, and cleanup. Comply with laboratory safety procedures, including appropriate use of personal protective equipment (PPE). Assist students with laboratory techniques and equipment operation while encouraging independent problem-solving. Help maintain laboratory inventory and notify the instructor when supplies need replenished. Clean and organize laboratory glassware, instruments, and work areas following each laboratory session. Assist with proper chemical waste collection and disposal in accordance with university and regulatory safety guidelines. Report equipment malfunctions, spills, or safety concerns promptly to the instructor. Maintain confidentiality regarding student records and grades. Required Qualifications: Successful completion of General Chemistry and at least one semester of Organic Chemistry. Ability to communicate effectively with students from a variety of academic backgrounds Dependable, punctual, and committed to maintaining a safe and professional laboratory environment. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience serving as a chemistry laboratory assistant, peer mentor, or tutor. Familiarity with introductory organic laboratory techniques, including: Measuring and transferring liquids and solids Filtration Liquid-liquid extraction Distillation Melting point determination Chromatography Safe handling of common organic solvents Physical Requirements: Ability to stand for extended periods during laboratory sessions. Ability to wear required personal protective equipment, including a laboratory coat, safety goggles, and gloves. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
