    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7887a8a03fc2be01a058a6815944b3&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Student Interns for Office for Civic Learning Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2385 # of Openings: 0 Student Intern for Civic Learning Dominican University Description: The Student Intern for Civic Learning works with the Director of Civic Learning to help coordinate all the functions of the Civic Learning Office, and to serve as a liaison between students, faculty, various community agencies, and the Civic Learning program at DU. Responsibilities: Civic Learning Office Tasks: Assist in the administrative tasks of running the Civic Learning Office, including providing clerical assistance to students, faculty, and community partners on DU Impact, the University’s electronic platform for community engagement. Assist in the updating of the Civic Learning web page, Facebook page, and EngageDU page. Attend weekly staff meeting. Prepare fliers, banners, and handouts for various Civic Learning events. Coordinate the Civic Learning EXPO (September/ January) Assist in the coordination of the Community-based Learning placement of students with agencies. Follow-up with student time logs, student evaluations and agency evaluations. Maintain data from Community-based Learning forms and compile a list of Community-based Learning students and their placements. Coordinate the annual Thanksgiving Basket Food Drive with St. Joseph Services (November) Serve as Liaison with Community Partners: Learn about the agency’s mission and work. Confirm the list of all student volunteers, times, email/ phone information with the agency supervisor. Update agency information on an ongoing basis through visiting their websites and inputting data collected during agency visits Report any difficulties or problems to the Civic Learning Director. Communicate with Community-based Learning Students: Work with students finding appropriate placements and getting them information about Community-based learning and the various agencies who are our community partners. Maintain communication with CBL students, informing them of “getting started” with their CBL placement, mid-term reminders and end-of-term forms and deadlines. Email CBL faculty with updates on students who face challenges with community engaged placement. Requirements: About 10 hours per week, either on site or in office. Some weeks will demand more time; some less. Responsible; personable; ability to follow through; good communication skills; flexibility; good people skills; passion for service and social justice. Should possess some knowledge of and experience with some community service agencies. Students must interview with the Civic Learning Director and student interns for the position. Must be eligible for student employment Must be registered at least part time in a degree-seeking program at Dominican University Compensation: 15.00/hour Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a06d0e20142fae&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "JOIN OUR TEAM",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Student Involvement Resource Center (SIRC) Staff Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2391 # of Openings: 1 TITLE: Student Involvement Resource Center (SIRC) Staff FLSA STATUS: Student Employee, up to 10 hours per week during academic year DEPARTMENT: Office of Student Involvement REPORTS TO: Office of Student Involvement Graduate Assistants and Professional Staff OPEN TO: Undergraduate Students PRIMARY PURPOSE/POSITION SUMMARY: Are you looking to be more involved on campus? Are you comfortable with being a little cringe? Do you value inclusive spaces on campus? Do you like meeting and engaging with new people? Becoming a SIRCL might be for you! You will serve as resource in the Student Involvement Resource Center (SIRC) and Underground spaces, manage resources, support programming, create marketing materials, provide information and support for student leaders and registered student organizations, monitor the Underground space, help in the promotion of our DUBeInvolved engagement platform, and assist the professional staff. You will also work to promote the mission and goals of the Office of Student Involvement. EXPECTATIONS FOR ALL DOMINICAN EMPLOYEES: To support the university's mission: pursue truth, give compassionate service, and participate in the creation of a more just and humane world. JOB COMPONENTS/PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: General Duties Serve as a welcoming front facing presence in the SIRC Assist Office of Student Involvement professional staff with department sponsored programs and events Maintain the publicity and promotional postings around campus Inventory of resources held within the SIRC and its storage facilities Late night and weekend work may be required Perform other duties as requested, delegated or assigned Student Involvement Resource Center (SIRC) and Underground Duties Create publicity and promotional materials for office sponsored events including banners, flyers, social media posts, and other formats Track the use of the SIRC and use of resources by the Dominican community Maintain and update bulletin boards and go on publicity runs Be a resource for student organizations, campus partners, and guests Commitment to keeping the space clean Monitoring the Underground throughout the day QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Reliable, creative and flexible Willingness to welcome new people into a space Possesses strong written, verbal, and organizational skills Must be kind, welcoming and inclusive Must be enrolled as an undergraduate student at Dominican at least part-time in a degree-seeking program Must be eligible for US employment If hired in the summer, applicants will be expected to attend a training before the beginning of the year Please reach out to jdaniels1@dom.edu with any questions! Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
